1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,200
and right now you're wondering why were kurda and asari mad at you i want you to find the answer

2
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:23,000
to that question figuring it out is your next assignment that feels so much better

3
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:30,840
what the hell man get up you're planning on just lying here all day it's monday and we only get one

4
00:00:30,840 --> 00:00:37,260
full day off all week you should take advantage of your free time while you can i'm fine not like

5
00:00:37,260 --> 00:00:38,880
there's any place i'm dying to go

6
00:02:10,004 --> 00:02:15,804
Well, I hope you're at least planning to get some proper rest over spring break.

7
00:02:16,264 --> 00:02:18,244
You know, if you're not planning to be going home.

8
00:02:18,624 --> 00:02:21,144
I'm just excited to finally be getting some laundry done, man.

9
00:02:21,384 --> 00:02:24,644
I feel bad having the dorm staff do it for me, so it piles up.

10
00:02:24,904 --> 00:02:28,704
I can't wait to get home and take advantage of my youth team status with all the ladies.

11
00:02:29,144 --> 00:02:29,904
Sounds fun.

12
00:02:30,284 --> 00:02:33,444
It's easy for us to visit our families, but I know it's harder for you.

13
00:02:34,164 --> 00:02:34,724
I'm sorry.

14
00:02:34,824 --> 00:02:36,284
It sucks to be you!

15
00:02:36,284 --> 00:02:40,624
It's cool. I'm fine.

16
00:02:41,044 --> 00:02:43,504
It'll be a good opportunity to find out more about everyone.

17
00:02:43,744 --> 00:02:46,484
I can sneak into your rooms and check out all your nudie mags.

18
00:02:46,604 --> 00:02:47,964
Don't you dare!

19
00:02:50,264 --> 00:02:53,304
Well, boys, I'm off to Shonen and Kanagawa.

20
00:02:53,644 --> 00:02:56,044
Most of my friends from home are getting together there.

21
00:02:56,204 --> 00:02:57,384
Oh, yeah? That's cool.

22
00:02:58,064 --> 00:03:01,764
Gotta be other guys from outside Tokyo who are here over break, right?

23
00:03:02,144 --> 00:03:05,964
That second-year Akutsu's family is somewhere outside the Kanto area.

24
00:03:06,284 --> 00:03:07,584
Maybe you could hang with him.

25
00:03:07,904 --> 00:03:08,824
Hell no!

26
00:03:10,184 --> 00:03:12,384
Don't even go there!

27
00:03:17,784 --> 00:03:20,824
I have so much I still have to pack up when I go home.

28
00:03:21,324 --> 00:03:22,224
Yeah, me too.

29
00:03:22,224 --> 00:03:24,224
Mm-hmm.

30
00:03:24,224 --> 00:03:42,564
Now that I think about it,

31
00:03:42,564 --> 00:03:44,984
I don't know much about the promoted players.

32
00:03:45,364 --> 00:03:48,244
I haven't really talked to any of them since the intra-squad game.

33
00:03:48,744 --> 00:03:51,304
But the type of pass should have clued you in.

34
00:03:51,664 --> 00:03:52,144
Owie!

35
00:03:52,484 --> 00:03:53,784
Pay attention to our movements!

36
00:03:55,484 --> 00:03:56,564
Is that why?

37
00:03:56,564 --> 00:04:01,904
Because I still haven't mastered all these skills that come naturally to them.

38
00:04:03,644 --> 00:04:06,444
I don't think they really see me as part of the team yet.

39
00:04:06,824 --> 00:04:08,064
And it sucks.

40
00:04:11,904 --> 00:04:14,084
Maybe I should give my friends back home a call.

41
00:04:14,084 --> 00:04:19,384
I can't.

42
00:04:19,844 --> 00:04:21,124
What would I even tell them?

43
00:04:27,844 --> 00:04:30,264
It's been almost a whole month.

44
00:04:30,604 --> 00:04:32,144
I haven't done anything yet.

45
00:04:35,464 --> 00:04:37,144
There's nothing to tell them.

46
00:04:37,144 --> 00:04:42,804
Shut up, wiener!

47
00:04:42,924 --> 00:04:44,204
Sitting around's no help!

48
00:04:44,504 --> 00:04:46,464
I'm gonna spend the whole day in training!

49
00:04:46,724 --> 00:04:47,064
Again!

50
00:04:47,444 --> 00:04:49,024
I don't care if it's our day off.

51
00:04:49,244 --> 00:04:51,224
I'll work hard and get better in all of them!

52
00:04:51,284 --> 00:04:51,684
Ashito?

53
00:04:56,544 --> 00:04:57,344
Oh, good!

54
00:04:57,504 --> 00:04:58,344
You're still here!

55
00:04:58,484 --> 00:04:59,684
Wanna come check out the high school?

56
00:05:00,064 --> 00:05:01,784
You haven't been to see it yet, have you?

57
00:05:02,104 --> 00:05:03,664
You're going to the same school as me,

58
00:05:03,704 --> 00:05:05,104
so I can show you around in advance?

59
00:05:05,224 --> 00:05:05,724
Come on!

60
00:05:06,284 --> 00:05:08,224
What the heck are you thinking, Hana?

61
00:05:08,444 --> 00:05:09,064
For real?

62
00:05:09,424 --> 00:05:11,144
First of all, this is a boys' dorm.

63
00:05:11,224 --> 00:05:13,324
You can't just barge in here like you own the place.

64
00:05:13,524 --> 00:05:14,844
Well, you don't have a cell phone,

65
00:05:14,924 --> 00:05:16,784
so how else am I supposed to contact you?

66
00:05:16,984 --> 00:05:18,964
I don't care about the stupid school.

67
00:05:19,184 --> 00:05:19,784
Let's go.

68
00:05:20,164 --> 00:05:20,944
I can't.

69
00:05:20,964 --> 00:05:22,184
I have stuff to do.

70
00:05:22,384 --> 00:05:22,824
Yeah, right.

71
00:05:25,964 --> 00:05:26,744
Oh, crap.

72
00:05:27,104 --> 00:05:29,744
I can't believe I forgot to put on cologne before I left.

73
00:05:29,904 --> 00:05:31,324
How am I going to bless the hotties?

74
00:05:31,344 --> 00:05:32,304
You're on the youth team.

75
00:05:32,464 --> 00:05:34,264
I figured you'd be stronger than this.

76
00:05:34,264 --> 00:05:36,264
Come on, put your back into it.

77
00:05:38,064 --> 00:05:38,464
What?

78
00:05:41,184 --> 00:05:42,504
You were bored, right?

79
00:05:45,644 --> 00:05:47,104
I rescued you, huh?

80
00:05:48,984 --> 00:05:50,104
Wasn't this a good call?

81
00:05:50,604 --> 00:05:52,124
Aren't you so glad I thought of it?

82
00:05:58,764 --> 00:06:00,144
At least say something!

83
00:06:00,144 --> 00:06:13,364
Are you trying to injure me here?

84
00:06:13,484 --> 00:06:13,924
Uh, what?

85
00:06:14,684 --> 00:06:15,744
That reminds me.

86
00:06:16,284 --> 00:06:18,104
I should probably give you this before I forget.

87
00:06:18,804 --> 00:06:19,484
Here you go.

88
00:06:19,484 --> 00:06:24,684
Um, I have no idea what this is.

89
00:06:25,064 --> 00:06:25,584
You better.

90
00:06:25,984 --> 00:06:27,224
It's your meal plan.

91
00:06:27,624 --> 00:06:28,004
What?

92
00:06:28,104 --> 00:06:28,804
Another one?

93
00:06:29,564 --> 00:06:30,824
Hey, listen up.

94
00:06:30,904 --> 00:06:33,104
If you want a strong body that isn't injury prone,

95
00:06:33,184 --> 00:06:34,224
you need to eat better.

96
00:06:34,724 --> 00:06:36,124
You made me one before.

97
00:06:36,504 --> 00:06:38,104
You don't have to keep on doing it, though.

98
00:06:38,564 --> 00:06:40,444
I'll eat whatever I want when I'm hungry.

99
00:06:40,444 --> 00:06:45,184
These are good for the next six months.

100
00:06:46,604 --> 00:06:48,084
So whenever you're ready,

101
00:06:48,364 --> 00:06:51,304
feel free to say thanks, Hana, so much.

102
00:06:52,364 --> 00:06:52,884
Interesting.

103
00:06:53,424 --> 00:06:55,224
Every time I see this girl,

104
00:06:55,524 --> 00:06:57,484
the same thought goes through my head.

105
00:06:57,644 --> 00:06:59,264
I can't help asking myself,

106
00:06:59,744 --> 00:07:02,804
where did this weirdo come from?

107
00:07:02,804 --> 00:07:05,524
You little sneak, Ashito.

108
00:07:05,764 --> 00:07:07,184
What the heck is going on here?

109
00:07:07,444 --> 00:07:10,144
When did you become so close to that tasty snack,

110
00:07:10,224 --> 00:07:11,484
and what the hell is she thinking?

111
00:07:15,184 --> 00:07:16,824
How long are you going to be around?

112
00:07:17,104 --> 00:07:19,184
Why don't you come hang out with the two of us instead?

113
00:07:20,184 --> 00:07:21,184
I'm back.

114
00:07:27,264 --> 00:07:28,484
You're pretty popular.

115
00:07:29,544 --> 00:07:30,184
Hold on.

116
00:07:30,344 --> 00:07:30,904
Where's yours?

117
00:07:31,144 --> 00:07:31,684
Not hungry?

118
00:07:31,684 --> 00:07:34,304
I'm just not really into desserts and stuff.

119
00:07:34,604 --> 00:07:35,144
It's cool.

120
00:07:35,784 --> 00:07:36,524
Good for you!

121
00:07:36,804 --> 00:07:38,164
Proper nutrition is important

122
00:07:38,164 --> 00:07:39,844
for growing professional athletes.

123
00:07:40,304 --> 00:07:41,804
Here's a fun factoid for you.

124
00:07:41,924 --> 00:07:43,104
When Zico came to Japan,

125
00:07:43,244 --> 00:07:44,424
he would always yell at players

126
00:07:44,424 --> 00:07:45,424
and call them unprofessional

127
00:07:45,424 --> 00:07:47,244
whenever they would forge themselves on junk.

128
00:07:48,424 --> 00:07:50,044
So what's the deal with you?

129
00:07:50,564 --> 00:07:52,204
You want to be a nutritionist or something?

130
00:07:53,344 --> 00:07:54,244
Or something.

131
00:07:55,024 --> 00:07:57,124
I want to be a doctor of sports medicine.

132
00:07:57,544 --> 00:07:59,464
That's why I have so many supplemental classes

133
00:07:59,464 --> 00:08:00,584
on my schedule every day.

134
00:08:00,584 --> 00:08:02,464
Keeps me busy, but it's cool.

135
00:08:02,864 --> 00:08:03,924
I'm a real hard worker.

136
00:08:04,724 --> 00:08:05,704
Sounds like it.

137
00:08:05,704 --> 00:08:08,384
Why were Kurata and Asari mad at you?

138
00:08:08,884 --> 00:08:10,644
I want you to find the answer to that question.

139
00:08:14,444 --> 00:08:16,604
You could at least pretend to be impressed.

140
00:08:17,424 --> 00:08:18,344
No, I am.

141
00:08:18,624 --> 00:08:19,284
I'm sorry.

142
00:08:19,664 --> 00:08:20,484
It's not you.

143
00:08:20,484 --> 00:08:23,144
This sucks.

144
00:08:23,484 --> 00:08:25,604
I can't focus on anything other than playing.

145
00:08:26,004 --> 00:08:27,644
I should be training right now.

146
00:08:28,104 --> 00:08:28,984
If I work at it,

147
00:08:29,044 --> 00:08:30,024
I know I can get better

148
00:08:30,024 --> 00:08:31,344
and prove to them that I belong.

149
00:08:31,724 --> 00:08:32,564
I have to.

150
00:08:32,564 --> 00:08:39,364
All right, here we are.

151
00:08:39,364 --> 00:08:41,564
Welcome to Tokyo Myosin High.

152
00:08:42,464 --> 00:08:45,424
So Tokyo Asperion is affiliated with this school,

153
00:08:45,844 --> 00:08:48,224
which means that anybody playing on the youth team

154
00:08:48,224 --> 00:08:50,084
who wants to go here can enroll on a scholarship.

155
00:08:50,344 --> 00:08:51,124
Pretty cool, huh?

156
00:08:51,824 --> 00:08:54,024
It makes the tuition super cheap,

157
00:08:54,144 --> 00:08:55,944
and it's easier to focus on soccer.

158
00:08:56,324 --> 00:08:57,944
All of the events and classes are scheduled

159
00:08:57,944 --> 00:08:59,064
around your training time.

160
00:08:59,064 --> 00:08:59,924
I know.

161
00:09:00,404 --> 00:09:01,704
It's because of the scholarship

162
00:09:01,704 --> 00:09:03,944
that my mom doesn't have to go bankrupt because of me.

163
00:09:04,264 --> 00:09:05,004
Well, I mean,

164
00:09:05,044 --> 00:09:06,984
you did move here from Ehime after all,

165
00:09:07,084 --> 00:09:09,144
so it's got to be a way bigger deal for you.

166
00:09:12,144 --> 00:09:13,884
I need to get back to my training.

167
00:09:14,444 --> 00:09:14,624
Huh?

168
00:09:15,384 --> 00:09:17,064
Glad I know how to get to school now.

169
00:09:17,664 --> 00:09:18,284
Thanks, Hana.

170
00:09:18,624 --> 00:09:19,024
Later.

171
00:09:19,264 --> 00:09:19,664
Wait!

172
00:09:24,664 --> 00:09:26,004
Rest days are important.

173
00:09:26,224 --> 00:09:26,824
Take them.

174
00:09:27,684 --> 00:09:27,884
Huh?

175
00:09:29,064 --> 00:09:30,324
You're training so much,

176
00:09:30,444 --> 00:09:32,404
but are you making all of those hours count?

177
00:09:33,444 --> 00:09:35,924
Charging in blindly doesn't achieve anything.

178
00:09:37,284 --> 00:09:38,324
Since I met you,

179
00:09:38,984 --> 00:09:41,764
I always admired the intense fire I saw in your eyes.

180
00:09:42,764 --> 00:09:44,404
But then there were other times,

181
00:09:45,004 --> 00:09:45,724
it was different.

182
00:09:46,604 --> 00:09:49,124
Those fiery eyes looked more angry and on edge.

183
00:09:49,724 --> 00:09:50,144
Yeah?

184
00:09:50,384 --> 00:09:51,544
Where's this coming from?

185
00:09:51,724 --> 00:09:53,244
Because you barely even know me.

186
00:09:53,504 --> 00:09:54,984
I know what I saw at the tryouts

187
00:09:54,984 --> 00:09:56,224
and in the intra-squad game.

188
00:09:56,224 --> 00:09:58,184
That dangerous look you get?

189
00:09:58,604 --> 00:10:00,724
Like you're about to self-destruct or something.

190
00:10:01,604 --> 00:10:02,804
It makes me worry.

191
00:10:05,024 --> 00:10:06,024
I'll tell you why.

192
00:10:09,244 --> 00:10:10,504
He was like that, too.

193
00:10:11,024 --> 00:10:13,024
My favorite player that you remind me of, I mean.

194
00:10:13,024 --> 00:10:17,344
Okay, look.

195
00:10:17,984 --> 00:10:20,284
You keep bringing up this favorite player of yours,

196
00:10:20,364 --> 00:10:22,184
but what am I supposed to do exactly?

197
00:10:22,584 --> 00:10:23,544
I don't get it!

198
00:10:25,204 --> 00:10:26,164
Nope, you sure don't.

199
00:10:26,164 --> 00:10:28,324
And another thing.

200
00:10:28,544 --> 00:10:30,064
Quit doing this kind of stuff.

201
00:10:30,184 --> 00:10:32,364
A pretty girl paying special attention to me?

202
00:10:32,704 --> 00:10:34,444
People are gonna get the wrong idea.

203
00:10:37,244 --> 00:10:38,924
I've had this body my whole life.

204
00:10:38,944 --> 00:10:39,864
I know its needs.

205
00:10:40,164 --> 00:10:41,484
You don't have to worry, okay?

206
00:10:41,564 --> 00:10:42,724
I'll be just fine.

207
00:10:42,724 --> 00:10:46,444
Look, I'm never gonna be this dude

208
00:10:46,444 --> 00:10:49,444
because I'm me, Ashito Aoi, genius forward.

209
00:10:49,604 --> 00:10:51,364
You're trying to turn me into someone else.

210
00:10:51,524 --> 00:10:52,184
Stop it!

211
00:10:52,244 --> 00:10:54,124
I'm not whoever this guy is, okay?

212
00:10:54,344 --> 00:10:55,664
Be delusional all you want,

213
00:10:55,724 --> 00:10:57,224
but leave me out of it!

214
00:10:58,224 --> 00:11:00,264
That's never what I was trying to do at all.

215
00:11:00,684 --> 00:11:03,044
All I wanted to do today was practice!

216
00:11:04,324 --> 00:11:05,964
If there's something I can't do,

217
00:11:06,044 --> 00:11:08,024
I have to master it as soon as I can.

218
00:11:08,824 --> 00:11:11,104
I've been watching the rest of the team play.

219
00:11:11,264 --> 00:11:13,324
I know how far behind I am.

220
00:11:13,704 --> 00:11:15,784
I've only got three years on this team.

221
00:11:15,944 --> 00:11:17,444
I'm on a time crunch here.

222
00:11:17,584 --> 00:11:19,344
I've been telling you I want to practice,

223
00:11:19,484 --> 00:11:21,084
so just let me do it!

224
00:11:21,164 --> 00:11:23,064
I appreciate you looking out for me,

225
00:11:23,484 --> 00:11:25,744
but you don't know what it's like to be on this side,

226
00:11:25,944 --> 00:11:28,024
so you really shouldn't be messing with...

227
00:11:30,384 --> 00:11:30,784
Huh?

228
00:11:30,784 --> 00:11:40,804
Hey, what about your bike?

229
00:11:40,804 --> 00:12:04,964
I knew it, man.

230
00:12:05,184 --> 00:12:08,304
I knew there was no way any girl would be hanging out with you

231
00:12:08,304 --> 00:12:09,764
because she actually liked you.

232
00:12:10,424 --> 00:12:11,224
Wait, what?

233
00:12:11,384 --> 00:12:12,224
You know something?

234
00:12:12,764 --> 00:12:15,064
You're kind of clueless when it comes to being aware

235
00:12:15,064 --> 00:12:16,264
of how other people feel.

236
00:12:17,044 --> 00:12:19,924
I noticed it yesterday while I was watching you in the game.

237
00:12:19,984 --> 00:12:20,244
Huh?

238
00:12:32,784 --> 00:12:36,104
Starting today, I hope you will dedicate yourselves to your studies

239
00:12:36,104 --> 00:12:38,944
and perfecting your skills as soon as you...

240
00:12:38,944 --> 00:12:40,944
Henri?

241
00:12:42,364 --> 00:12:43,264
No way.

242
00:12:43,424 --> 00:12:45,344
I never thought I'd run into you at this school.

243
00:12:45,504 --> 00:12:47,724
You seem too smart to go to a place like this.

244
00:12:49,904 --> 00:12:53,204
Yes, well, if I want to end up in my chosen profession,

245
00:12:53,724 --> 00:12:56,324
I figured it would be best for me to attend the same school

246
00:12:56,324 --> 00:12:57,204
that the players do.

247
00:12:57,704 --> 00:13:00,304
You really are quite the strange one, aren't you?

248
00:13:02,224 --> 00:13:03,624
Whoa, Yuma, wait a second.

249
00:13:04,044 --> 00:13:04,764
What's the deal?

250
00:13:04,764 --> 00:13:06,564
Hey, man, the deal?

251
00:13:06,784 --> 00:13:07,404
What do you mean?

252
00:13:08,344 --> 00:13:11,324
Um, isn't that the daughter of Asperion's sponsor?

253
00:13:11,704 --> 00:13:13,584
Do you really know her well enough to joke with her?

254
00:13:14,044 --> 00:13:17,544
Dude, my mom's been a house cleaner for her family for ages.

255
00:13:18,024 --> 00:13:19,304
I know her just fine.

256
00:13:19,924 --> 00:13:22,484
She and I go way back to when we were snot-nosed kids.

257
00:13:23,364 --> 00:13:25,204
So, you check out the class yet?

258
00:13:25,284 --> 00:13:27,844
A pretty interesting lineup we've got here, don't you think?

259
00:13:27,844 --> 00:13:35,624
There's me, you, Takeshima, Asari, Kuroda, Togashi, and...

260
00:13:35,624 --> 00:13:43,044
I noticed it yesterday while I was watching you in the game.

261
00:13:43,344 --> 00:13:45,184
Um, I don't get it.

262
00:13:45,684 --> 00:13:47,364
What do you mean, Otomo, huh?

263
00:13:47,364 --> 00:13:52,364
No, I'll...

264
00:13:52,364 --> 00:13:54,604
I'll just think it over.

265
00:14:01,804 --> 00:14:03,684
Peek-a-boo, Ashito, Aoi.

266
00:14:03,884 --> 00:14:05,364
It's been ten days.

267
00:14:05,764 --> 00:14:07,064
Have you found your answer?

268
00:14:09,764 --> 00:14:12,304
Ashito, I heard you made Hana cry the other day.

269
00:14:12,304 --> 00:14:14,184
Man, too quick to make a move.

270
00:14:14,364 --> 00:14:15,724
And even quicker to get dumped.

271
00:14:16,744 --> 00:14:19,964
If you were wondering, Hana Ichijo is not in our class.

272
00:14:20,244 --> 00:14:21,804
Sorry if that crushes your dreams.

273
00:14:22,564 --> 00:14:25,264
According to my investigative notes on cute girls here,

274
00:14:26,284 --> 00:14:27,924
she's in Advanced English.

275
00:14:28,244 --> 00:14:29,564
And it's in a different building,

276
00:14:29,684 --> 00:14:31,904
so you probably won't see her around much.

277
00:14:35,304 --> 00:14:38,724
You know, when you make girls cry, you've got 24 hours.

278
00:14:38,984 --> 00:14:40,504
To apologize, that is.

279
00:14:40,504 --> 00:14:42,824
That's what all my research says, anyway.

280
00:14:43,184 --> 00:14:45,404
It's been ten days now, hasn't it?

281
00:14:45,664 --> 00:14:47,644
I guess the love story's over.

282
00:14:58,644 --> 00:15:01,104
You're obviously struggling with something over here.

283
00:15:01,584 --> 00:15:03,764
Just don't drag it out till the start of the league.

284
00:15:04,124 --> 00:15:07,904
I mean, the B team plays competitive matches, too, you know?

285
00:15:07,904 --> 00:15:10,504
That's what's great about the youth team.

286
00:15:10,904 --> 00:15:14,124
It's a small enough number that we get more chances to play than usual.

287
00:15:14,664 --> 00:15:16,944
The B team actually plays in a league, too,

288
00:15:17,044 --> 00:15:19,764
so you can rack up some game time along with the rest of us.

289
00:15:20,764 --> 00:15:22,804
So then, we compete, too?

290
00:15:22,804 --> 00:15:35,444
Right.

291
00:15:41,324 --> 00:15:42,404
I don't get it.

292
00:15:42,404 --> 00:15:47,004
I'm saying that I get that I don't get it now.

293
00:15:47,684 --> 00:15:48,624
Okay, whatever.

294
00:15:49,284 --> 00:15:50,484
I don't want to talk to you.

295
00:15:50,944 --> 00:15:51,844
Leave us alone.

296
00:15:52,444 --> 00:15:53,164
I'm an idiot.

297
00:15:53,544 --> 00:15:54,444
You know that.

298
00:15:54,824 --> 00:15:57,544
I have no idea what you're thinking unless you tell me.

299
00:15:57,664 --> 00:15:59,844
But still, that kind of came out of nowhere.

300
00:16:00,584 --> 00:16:02,204
Sure, it was totally my bad.

301
00:16:02,684 --> 00:16:03,864
But did you have to cry?

302
00:16:04,584 --> 00:16:05,004
What?

303
00:16:05,004 --> 00:16:10,144
Also, I don't understand why all of us can't just get along.

304
00:16:10,764 --> 00:16:13,164
And there's not much I can do about something I don't get.

305
00:16:13,844 --> 00:16:15,144
So let's talk it through.

306
00:16:18,224 --> 00:16:19,784
First, the 11 on 21.

307
00:16:20,444 --> 00:16:22,644
You want to know what I was thinking during that play?

308
00:16:22,864 --> 00:16:25,124
I'll tell you what was going through my head.

309
00:16:25,544 --> 00:16:27,884
I wanted to hold it up at the front of the goal

310
00:16:27,884 --> 00:16:29,244
and then pass it out to the wing.

311
00:16:29,384 --> 00:16:30,564
Then turn and run.

312
00:16:30,564 --> 00:16:32,904
That's when I'd get him behind Akutsu,

313
00:16:33,084 --> 00:16:34,284
pick up the return pass,

314
00:16:34,444 --> 00:16:35,884
and shoot and score from there.

315
00:16:36,904 --> 00:16:38,084
So there you go.

316
00:16:38,264 --> 00:16:39,924
That's what I was thinking at the time.

317
00:16:40,464 --> 00:16:42,424
But I was up against Akutsu.

318
00:16:43,964 --> 00:16:45,304
So from your perspective,

319
00:16:45,644 --> 00:16:46,984
you didn't think I could handle it.

320
00:16:47,164 --> 00:16:48,704
You thought I couldn't get past him.

321
00:16:49,224 --> 00:16:49,784
That it?

322
00:16:50,084 --> 00:16:52,244
You got upset with me because I was too reckless?

323
00:16:53,464 --> 00:16:55,764
I've had 10 days to think about this.

324
00:16:55,764 --> 00:16:58,264
And it's the scenario that makes the most sense.

325
00:16:58,584 --> 00:17:00,204
I have no idea if I'm right.

326
00:17:00,204 --> 00:17:01,584
But I do know this.

327
00:17:02,224 --> 00:17:04,084
I want to get out on the field together

328
00:17:04,084 --> 00:17:05,664
and score some goals.

329
00:17:05,884 --> 00:17:06,364
Don't you?

330
00:17:07,084 --> 00:17:08,464
All I've been thinking about

331
00:17:08,464 --> 00:17:09,804
is how to make that happen.

332
00:17:10,664 --> 00:17:12,064
Anyway, that's all I've got.

333
00:17:12,184 --> 00:17:13,224
I've said my piece.

334
00:17:13,424 --> 00:17:14,204
Now you.

335
00:17:17,204 --> 00:17:18,564
Like you said before,

336
00:17:18,884 --> 00:17:19,764
it might take a while

337
00:17:19,764 --> 00:17:21,524
for this year's first years to get along.

338
00:17:23,284 --> 00:17:25,884
We've got quite a few characters this time, don't we?

339
00:17:26,364 --> 00:17:28,504
The promoted players are conscientious,

340
00:17:28,504 --> 00:17:30,644
while Aoi and the others are more relaxed.

341
00:17:31,304 --> 00:17:33,244
They're not on the same page at all.

342
00:17:34,204 --> 00:17:35,224
Especially Aoi.

343
00:17:35,544 --> 00:17:37,384
Are you sure this is the right way to do it?

344
00:17:38,644 --> 00:17:39,004
Fukuda,

345
00:17:39,204 --> 00:17:42,184
your coaching methods have worked so well up to now.

346
00:17:42,184 --> 00:17:45,064
Maybe if our advice was more direct...

347
00:17:45,064 --> 00:17:45,724
Bad idea.

348
00:17:46,724 --> 00:17:47,124
Nozomi,

349
00:17:47,804 --> 00:17:49,504
that only make you feel better.

350
00:17:50,144 --> 00:17:52,284
Giving players all the answers right away.

351
00:17:52,584 --> 00:17:54,144
That's just the lazy approach.

352
00:17:55,984 --> 00:17:57,624
They have to use their brains.

353
00:17:58,204 --> 00:17:58,984
That's the point.

354
00:18:00,564 --> 00:18:02,664
Aoi's case is particularly delicate.

355
00:18:02,664 --> 00:18:05,684
I just hope things work out

356
00:18:05,684 --> 00:18:06,964
the way you say they will.

357
00:18:08,364 --> 00:18:09,764
He's on the B-team, Nozomi.

358
00:18:10,124 --> 00:18:11,564
So it's on you for now.

359
00:18:12,324 --> 00:18:13,884
Everybody knows that a coach

360
00:18:13,884 --> 00:18:15,384
can make or break their players.

361
00:18:15,864 --> 00:18:16,704
Ashito, well,

362
00:18:17,164 --> 00:18:18,404
he'll figure out the answer.

363
00:18:19,064 --> 00:18:21,824
Even if he does take the long way around to do it.

364
00:18:21,824 --> 00:18:25,884
That sounds great.

365
00:18:26,024 --> 00:18:27,364
You want to have a soccer discussion?

366
00:18:28,004 --> 00:18:28,864
I'm interested.

367
00:18:29,324 --> 00:18:29,944
Thanks, Aoi.

368
00:18:30,184 --> 00:18:31,084
What the hell, man?

369
00:18:31,624 --> 00:18:32,824
So, we're talking about

370
00:18:32,824 --> 00:18:35,084
the 11-on-21 game we had last week, huh?

371
00:18:35,304 --> 00:18:36,284
Uh, yeah.

372
00:18:37,304 --> 00:18:37,744
Okay.

373
00:18:38,244 --> 00:18:40,884
I didn't expect him to be so open to talking about it.

374
00:18:41,104 --> 00:18:41,904
In that case,

375
00:18:42,484 --> 00:18:43,784
looks like it's still your turn.

376
00:18:44,164 --> 00:18:44,364
Huh?

377
00:18:45,284 --> 00:18:46,124
I'm curious.

378
00:18:46,824 --> 00:18:48,204
You must have had ideas

379
00:18:48,204 --> 00:18:49,544
on how to score in that moment

380
00:18:49,544 --> 00:18:51,464
that didn't involve taking on Akutsu,

381
00:18:51,464 --> 00:18:51,904
right?

382
00:18:54,664 --> 00:18:55,744
Yeah, duh.

383
00:18:56,244 --> 00:18:57,144
They want to know.

384
00:18:57,364 --> 00:18:58,684
I can talk to them about it.

385
00:18:59,384 --> 00:19:00,544
Okay, check this out.

386
00:19:00,584 --> 00:19:02,224
My first idea involved a crosser.

387
00:19:02,424 --> 00:19:03,804
I would have passed to Tachibana

388
00:19:03,804 --> 00:19:04,704
on the left here.

389
00:19:05,044 --> 00:19:06,064
Then he would have sent it

390
00:19:06,064 --> 00:19:07,064
to the opposite wing.

391
00:19:08,324 --> 00:19:10,044
That's when I would have made a run

392
00:19:10,044 --> 00:19:10,844
into the middle.

393
00:19:11,204 --> 00:19:12,244
Overlapping on the right,

394
00:19:12,444 --> 00:19:14,304
Asuri would have sent in the cross.

395
00:19:14,984 --> 00:19:15,864
And then,

396
00:19:16,184 --> 00:19:17,284
I would have scored.

397
00:19:19,924 --> 00:19:20,724
I'm following.

398
00:19:20,724 --> 00:19:22,104
There was some space

399
00:19:22,104 --> 00:19:23,084
on the right at the time,

400
00:19:23,144 --> 00:19:23,504
you see.

401
00:19:24,264 --> 00:19:25,224
It's so cool

402
00:19:25,224 --> 00:19:27,044
that I can talk about soccer like this,

403
00:19:27,164 --> 00:19:28,484
even if I'm not on the field.

404
00:19:29,004 --> 00:19:29,824
My second thought

405
00:19:29,824 --> 00:19:30,784
was to offload it.

406
00:19:31,284 --> 00:19:32,824
Like to Roland or Tachibana

407
00:19:32,824 --> 00:19:33,584
in front of the goal.

408
00:19:34,064 --> 00:19:35,164
Then a bunch of us

409
00:19:35,164 --> 00:19:36,564
could have run towards the keeper.

410
00:19:36,904 --> 00:19:38,164
That would confuse the crap

411
00:19:38,164 --> 00:19:39,064
out of the opposition.

412
00:19:39,604 --> 00:19:41,124
Since I was closest to the goal,

413
00:19:41,344 --> 00:19:43,164
someone could have hit a long pass to me,

414
00:19:43,244 --> 00:19:44,464
and I would have scored.

415
00:19:44,464 --> 00:19:48,004
In the end,

416
00:19:48,064 --> 00:19:49,024
they're just like me.

417
00:19:49,144 --> 00:19:50,424
They all love soccer.

418
00:19:50,724 --> 00:19:52,504
Maybe now we can understand each other.

419
00:19:52,724 --> 00:19:53,564
My third idea

420
00:19:53,564 --> 00:19:54,844
was a bit more unlikely.

421
00:19:55,324 --> 00:19:56,304
But before Akutsu

422
00:19:56,304 --> 00:19:57,204
had time to get to me,

423
00:19:57,284 --> 00:19:57,904
I could have fainted

424
00:19:57,904 --> 00:19:59,024
and passed to Tachibana.

425
00:19:59,224 --> 00:20:00,304
But then aimed at the goal

426
00:20:00,304 --> 00:20:01,564
instead and scored, huh?

427
00:20:01,584 --> 00:20:02,224
That's enough.

428
00:20:02,964 --> 00:20:04,024
Just stop.

429
00:20:05,024 --> 00:20:07,084
Why do all these brilliant ideas

430
00:20:07,084 --> 00:20:08,624
end with you scoring, huh?

431
00:20:08,624 --> 00:20:14,924
Tell you what.

432
00:20:15,304 --> 00:20:17,424
Stop obsessing over scoring the goals,

433
00:20:17,584 --> 00:20:19,104
then maybe we can talk.

434
00:20:19,824 --> 00:20:21,444
I agree on that point.

435
00:20:21,824 --> 00:20:23,344
It sure would make a huge difference

436
00:20:23,344 --> 00:20:24,384
if you were asking me

437
00:20:24,384 --> 00:20:26,164
to thrive on the youth team.

438
00:20:26,264 --> 00:20:27,144
Hold on a second.

439
00:20:28,264 --> 00:20:30,364
Is that it?

440
00:20:30,784 --> 00:20:31,764
Is that the reason

441
00:20:31,764 --> 00:20:32,984
you two got mad at me?

442
00:20:34,404 --> 00:20:35,944
Are you kidding me?

443
00:20:36,224 --> 00:20:37,664
I'm a Ford, you guys.

444
00:20:37,664 --> 00:20:39,204
Why wouldn't I be thinking

445
00:20:39,204 --> 00:20:40,004
about scoring?

446
00:20:41,204 --> 00:20:43,384
Stop obsessing over scoring goals.

447
00:20:43,544 --> 00:20:44,364
The moment a forward

448
00:20:44,364 --> 00:20:45,464
starts thinking like that,

449
00:20:45,624 --> 00:20:46,244
he's done.

450
00:20:46,504 --> 00:20:48,344
The whole point of coming to Asperion

451
00:20:48,344 --> 00:20:48,924
was to become

452
00:20:48,924 --> 00:20:50,404
the best forward in the world.

453
00:20:50,624 --> 00:20:52,084
Well then, good for you.

454
00:20:52,364 --> 00:20:53,284
I still don't even know

455
00:20:53,284 --> 00:20:54,844
how you made it on the youth team.

456
00:20:55,104 --> 00:20:56,764
It really pisses me off

457
00:20:56,764 --> 00:20:58,644
thinking about my junior teammates

458
00:20:58,644 --> 00:20:59,484
who didn't make it

459
00:20:59,484 --> 00:21:01,364
because you stole their spot.

460
00:21:02,484 --> 00:21:03,944
What are you talking about?

461
00:21:04,344 --> 00:21:05,024
Stole it?

462
00:21:05,424 --> 00:21:05,804
Otomo,

463
00:21:05,804 --> 00:21:08,104
this has nothing to do with you.

464
00:21:08,464 --> 00:21:09,384
Ashito and I fought

465
00:21:09,384 --> 00:21:10,324
alongside each other

466
00:21:10,324 --> 00:21:10,964
at the tryouts

467
00:21:10,964 --> 00:21:12,444
with our careers on the line.

468
00:21:13,264 --> 00:21:14,204
We fought hard.

469
00:21:15,384 --> 00:21:16,604
Failure wasn't an option

470
00:21:16,604 --> 00:21:18,144
and we had to go through hell.

471
00:21:19,104 --> 00:21:20,664
If you've got a problem with that,

472
00:21:20,724 --> 00:21:21,744
I won't stay quiet.

473
00:21:21,924 --> 00:21:23,024
As for taking a spot

474
00:21:23,024 --> 00:21:24,084
away from your teammates,

475
00:21:24,644 --> 00:21:26,044
that's a bunch of crap

476
00:21:26,044 --> 00:21:26,884
and you know it.

477
00:21:26,884 --> 00:21:28,564
Get over yourself, Asari.

478
00:21:29,104 --> 00:21:30,424
We earned our spots

479
00:21:30,424 --> 00:21:31,264
and you know it.

480
00:21:31,264 --> 00:21:32,824
Takashima,

481
00:21:33,184 --> 00:21:33,504
Kurada,

482
00:21:33,604 --> 00:21:34,304
let go!

483
00:21:35,304 --> 00:21:35,864
Asari,

484
00:21:36,264 --> 00:21:37,664
what Otomo's saying is true.

485
00:21:38,164 --> 00:21:39,064
You went too far.

486
00:21:40,084 --> 00:21:41,404
You can't say that.

487
00:21:41,404 --> 00:21:54,304
I can't believe it.

488
00:21:54,484 --> 00:21:55,524
They were pissed off at me

489
00:21:55,524 --> 00:21:56,324
because I was focused

490
00:21:56,324 --> 00:21:57,184
on being a Ford

491
00:21:57,184 --> 00:21:58,124
and making goals.

492
00:21:58,344 --> 00:21:59,424
That's just ridiculous.

493
00:22:00,704 --> 00:22:01,424
No way.

494
00:22:02,084 --> 00:22:03,264
That can't be all of it.

495
00:22:03,724 --> 00:22:04,924
It just doesn't feel right.

496
00:22:05,704 --> 00:22:06,644
There must be more

497
00:22:06,644 --> 00:22:07,464
to what they said.

498
00:22:07,464 --> 00:22:10,564
Coach Nozomi!

499
00:22:11,544 --> 00:22:12,684
There you are, Ali.

500
00:22:13,104 --> 00:22:13,464
Good.

501
00:22:14,044 --> 00:22:15,724
I actually wanted to talk to you

502
00:22:15,724 --> 00:22:17,264
because next week,

503
00:22:17,784 --> 00:22:18,904
you'll be a starter.

504
00:22:20,664 --> 00:22:21,144
However,

505
00:22:21,644 --> 00:22:23,244
I need to see you make a play

506
00:22:23,244 --> 00:22:24,424
that proves you completed

507
00:22:24,424 --> 00:22:25,704
the assignment I set you.

508
00:22:26,504 --> 00:22:27,804
If you can't do that,

509
00:22:28,184 --> 00:22:29,524
I won't field you in a match

510
00:22:29,524 --> 00:22:30,684
for the next three months.

511
00:22:31,564 --> 00:22:32,984
So act as if your life

512
00:22:32,984 --> 00:22:33,824
depends on it.

513
00:24:05,986 --> 00:24:28,306
Next time on Aorashi, Tokyo Metropolis League Match 1, Seikyo High School.

